<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,095.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,095.</headline>
<text>
<p>Spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,095 today from 1,076 on Oct 15, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route			   Index    Rate    Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1   US GULF/ARA	  1200    10.892    1152    10.457</p>
<p>   1a  TRANSATLANTIC RV   0988  7483.000    0956  7243.000</p>
<p>   2   US GULF/JAPAN	1473    21.042    1458    20.836</p>
<p>   2a  SKAW P/USG/F EAST  1197  9817.000    1156  9479.000</p>
<p>   3   NOPAC/JAPAN	  1282    11.825    1260    11.629</p>
<p>   3a  JAPAN-SK/NOPAC/RV  1014  8000.000    1007  7950.000</p>
<p>   6   HR OR HR-RB/JAPAN  1116    11.507    1111    11.456</p>
<p>   7   HR/ROTTERDAM	 1011     4.921    1008     4.906</p>
<p>   8   QLAND/ROTTERDAM    0702     7.714    0702     7.719</p>
